{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1807 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e1b3ba9721471f103070078d92b56772f3b44da9a7e497d32d6329bb95a15578" :edb/db-before-t 1806 :edb/db-after-t 1807 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535119 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:18:00.821Z" 13194139535119 true] [17592186192611 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332158 13194139535119 true] [17592186192612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332165 13194139535119 true] [17592186192612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332172 13194139535119 true] [17592186192612 1020 #edb/ref 17592186332179 13194139535119 true] [17592186193040 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535119 true] [17592186193040 1100 "Consider the set $A$, defined by\n$A = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: y < 1 - x}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n2. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n3. $intA = A$" 13194139535119 false] [17592186193040 1100 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139535119 true] [17592186193040 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332158 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332159 13194139535119 true] [17592186332158 1089 "q-161624" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332158 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535119 true] [17592186332158 1100 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332158 1113 #uuid "318629c1-2457-50a8-91b8-67b30dc4061b" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332158 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8414de2e05da43c03fae3c8b1ff2102401e990188e9fd4ee59a24308ec34b086.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we have seen, $∂A$ consists of two concentric circles: the outer one is in $A,$ while the inner one is not.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains some of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332160 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332161 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332162 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332163 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332164 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1041 "selection" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332164 13194139535119 true] [17592186332159 1110 #uuid "6ad2ca6b-d482-5608-9f02-2e57e713f54b" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332160 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535119 true] [17592186332160 1111 #uuid "bc6718f6-4976-57b6-b370-f79e3466cb78" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332161 1034 "I only" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535119 true] [17592186332161 1111 #uuid "3eda1123-fb27-58ee-b348-baf8461c20c7" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332162 1034 "III only" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535119 true] [17592186332162 1111 #uuid "0c1363c9-8a00-510f-a8af-9a584d6f4f2a" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332163 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535119 true] [17592186332163 1111 #uuid "f3aed6ca-2b03-5dde-a451-aa62b960f5b9" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332164 1034 "II only" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535119 true] [17592186332164 1111 #uuid "9be9472c-4118-5314-9f01-1e88064b98a5" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332165 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332166 13194139535119 true] [17592186332165 1089 "q-161718" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332165 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535119 true] [17592186332165 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/af1e6e7b384732a527fc77e9729c6e02aaa288d4076c030c9fae58742cb10f74.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332165 1113 #uuid "9cae3814-ea99-54e9-86e7-c0bc019bdf37" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332165 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/0a0b92621d83d6395926a75b5cae34f479a8b9e64dfe82711094c3724b3b3220.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/3ddef68bf4b4284c1b68896920fddb8d7fb0e70eba15dee103cdbc0134a9ed20.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-x<y<x}.\n$$" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332167 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332168 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332169 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332170 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332171 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1041 "selection" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332170 13194139535119 true] [17592186332166 1110 #uuid "85c065e2-d4a7-5f6e-aa29-d60489c19beb" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332167 1034 "0<y\\le x" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332167 1111 #uuid "07cb221d-6254-54c9-b93b-66f9c21ca222" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332168 1034 "-x\\le y\\le x" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332168 1111 #uuid "6f724aae-8b8f-5b82-bac0-67f022cb60ea" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332169 1034 "-x\\le y<x" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332169 1111 #uuid "1befd6ec-4f43-5a5a-90de-6227f6e4bdee" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332170 1034 "-x<y<x" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332170 1111 #uuid "fd49e677-9cf8-59d2-abc2-ae8a5ae11b85" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332171 1034 "0<y<x" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332171 1111 #uuid "1f006973-3acf-581b-842a-d7f56833fef0" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332172 1017 #edb/ref 17592186332173 13194139535119 true] [17592186332172 1089 "q-161730" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332172 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535119 true] [17592186332172 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/aa335a55f5b4496cdaccca5d35e286a168598761188bc520c81397ef136f927d.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332172 1113 #uuid "02d084df-878c-5b52-8acb-7b7ee4dbdd09" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332172 1145 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/fba9ba3e52ed19eb0bb2286ae59c49bb9dc648134d9eab3c4e2d13862963f736.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/2f3cd30dbaa4f84c43f2a7f1197aa904e3d43b1212241ae26736b2a0087f6170.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332174 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332175 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332176 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332177 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332178 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1041 "selection" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332174 13194139535119 true] [17592186332173 1110 #uuid "c9210ab2-eeb9-5f7b-b9eb-272b79a0921a" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332174 1034 "0<y<2" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332174 1111 #uuid "0da8d515-7cc0-506d-abb2-6c7a21926771" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332175 1034 "-1\\le y\\le 1" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332175 1111 #uuid "4c2617a0-7b87-51fe-9e98-a57527022afa" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332176 1034 "0\\le y\\le 2" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332176 1111 #uuid "2f2db1fd-ef9f-52cf-8fd2-c24e6c710a89" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332177 1034 "y=0" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332177 1111 #uuid "8761eec8-3cc6-5877-b192-11245ef0e21c" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332178 1034 "y=2" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535119 true] [17592186332178 1111 #uuid "fb486883-b547-52d1-b198-5104c36a9bbf" 13194139535119 true] [17592186332179 1017 #e